---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"library\", \"pull\"])"
---
Read the enabled profiles of the pad, live, and write them as KDL (needs control channel v1.4 of the gamepadii firmware). It reads only: it changes nothing on the pad

Usage: gamepadii library pull [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --write [<FILE>]
          Write the KDL into a file, not to standard output. A file name with no directory goes into the library [default: the board name, for example haute42-s16.kdl]

      --force
          Replace the file when it is there

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --names <SYSTEM>
          The names of the actions: gp2040 (B1, S2), xbox (A, Start), playstation (Cross, Options) or switch (B, Plus)
          
          [default: gp2040]
          [possible values: gp2040, xbox, playstation, switch]

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
